From b73b71f84ce7b6fb7c3889a73c63d6ea0d4c4a60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolas <199779756+nicopingu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:56:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] In-memory LoRA, applied as each DiT block is loaded (--lora
 FILE@FORCE, repeatable)

W += force * up @ down_t^T on qkv, out, fc1 and fc2 of the 50 blocks and the token refiner, computed in F32
(MPSGraph) then rounded once to BF16, as a fusion on disk does: on a 22-frame Turbo video the MP4 is byte-for-byte
identical to the one rendered from the fused transformer. Several LoRA are concatenated along the rank. With
--ssd-streaming the update is applied at each read of the block; resident, once at load. Files in the
h3-lora-natif format, written by PLI's tools/pli-lora-natif.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
